# upright — a walking E-minor line on the GarageBand musical-typing map (2026-08-21).
#
# READ THIS IF AN A/B ON THIS CART COMES BACK BYTE-IDENTICAL: `script /dev/null` renders
# DIGITAL SILENCE (peak -inf). upright is a played instrument, not a sequencer — there is
# no transport to start, so a render with no input has no notes in it. ab-render then blames
# the flag ("did not reach the DSP") for what is really an empty take.
#
# The map (upright.c:94-99): KB_ROOT 28, 'A' = E1 at octave 0, white keys "ASDFGHJKL;'" at
# semitones 0 2 4 5 7 9 11 12 14 16 17, black keys WETYUOP at 1 3 6 8 10 13 15.
# So E minor pentatonic (0 3 5 7 10) is A E F G U — that is the line below, 4 notes per bar,
# 30 frames apart (=120bpm quarters at 60fps) held 26 frames for a legato pizz.
# Mono, last-note-wins, so the holds must not overlap.
down 12 A
up 38 A
